WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.360 --> 00:00:01.920
The A to Z of -isms...

00:00:02.000 --> 00:00:03.720
transhumanism.

00:00:03.800 --> 00:00:07.840
Most of us would consider the end
of the human race as a catastrophe.

00:00:09.280 --> 00:00:12.200
There are some however
who would not only rejoice at it

00:00:12.280 --> 00:00:15.120
but want to hasten the day it arrives.

00:00:15.680 --> 00:00:19.520
Transhumanists look forward to a future
in which Homo sapiens

00:00:19.600 --> 00:00:23.400
is superseded by a better,
smarter, fitter model -

00:00:23.480 --> 00:00:25.640
humanity 2.0.

00:00:25.720 --> 00:00:28.600
Humans are in dire need of improvement.

00:00:28.680 --> 00:00:32.320
Any species that causes
huge damage to our environment,

00:00:32.400 --> 00:00:35.080
can't feed itself
even though it has enough food

00:00:35.160 --> 00:00:38.360
and fights countless wars
costing millions of lives

00:00:38.440 --> 00:00:41.480
must surely benefit
from an intelligence upgrade.

00:00:41.560 --> 00:00:43.120
Our lifespans are short,

00:00:43.200 --> 00:00:47.680
our final years usually characterised
by diminishing health and vitality,

00:00:47.760 --> 00:00:50.880
often accompanied
by a drop off in cognitive capacity.

00:00:50.960 --> 00:00:55.680
One in three people born in 2015
are expected to get dementia.

00:00:55.760 --> 00:00:58.240
Is this really the best we can hope for?

00:00:58.320 --> 00:01:00.200
Transhumanists think not.

00:01:00.720 --> 00:01:03.840
Ageing could be stopped
and even reversed.

00:01:03.920 --> 00:01:06.840
Enhancements
could dramatically raise our IQs

00:01:06.920 --> 00:01:09.160
and make us stronger and fitter.

00:01:10.000 --> 00:01:13.280
We might even be able
to leave our fragile bodies behind

00:01:13.360 --> 00:01:18.080
and upload ourselves to computers,
living forever in virtual worlds.

00:01:18.600 --> 00:01:21.320
Improving humanity
through science and technology

00:01:21.400 --> 00:01:22.800
could radically change us.

00:01:22.880 --> 00:01:27.480
Such a new beginning would in effect
be the end of humanity as we know it.

00:01:27.560 --> 00:01:32.040
Many transhumanists see this
as not only desirable but inevitable.

00:01:32.120 --> 00:01:34.560
The scientist and futurist, Ray Kurzweil,

00:01:34.640 --> 00:01:37.680
believes we are approaching
what he calls "the singularity" -

00:01:37.760 --> 00:01:41.720
the point at which computers become
smart enough to learn for themselves,

00:01:41.800 --> 00:01:45.480
after which they will rapidly
become smarter and smarter.

00:01:45.560 --> 00:01:48.640
The future belongs
to artificial intelligence.

00:01:48.720 --> 00:01:52.000
The only way for humanity to survive
is to embrace it

00:01:52.080 --> 00:01:55.200
and become
wholly or partially artificial ourselves.

00:01:55.880 --> 00:01:58.960
The thought of being replaced
by a new form of humanity

00:01:59.040 --> 00:02:00.880
is bound to be unsettling.

00:02:00.960 --> 00:02:02.440
But transhumanists think

00:02:02.520 --> 00:02:06.040
we would be wrong to lament
the end of humanity as we know it

00:02:06.120 --> 00:02:09.000
when what replaces us
would be so much better.

00:02:09.080 --> 00:02:11.360
It would be like wishing
children never grew up

00:02:11.440 --> 00:02:15.040
or that Homo erectus never evolved
into Homo sapiens.

00:02:15.120 --> 00:02:17.160
If the transhumanists are right,

00:02:17.240 --> 00:02:21.560
we could be one of the last generations
of humans to roam the planet.

00:02:25.420 --> 00:02:26.720
Thanks for watching.

00:02:26.720 --> 00:02:30.700
Don't forget to subscribe and click the bell to receive notifications for new videos.

00:02:30.700 --> 00:02:32.120
See you again soon!

